 resident & CEO\nNCX Group\, Inc\nOffice: 888-448-5451\nCell: 714-931-545
 8\n[id:image001.png@01D32C93.C3E73300]\nBook Some Time With Me<https://c
 alendly.com/ncxgroup>\nVisit Our Site<https://linkprotect.cudasvc.com/ur
 l?a=http%3a%2f%2fwww.ncxgroup.com%2f&c=E\,1\,am0iUeysQL-vZUeGaz9ktryJpfW
 CT-Mw6gKVSKL8nTKnKVwbBxdrRq5dkLvH0kITOjYvAcoXdUIvqm9eNpMQGe0Ig-BmgA0avep
 p0K8hFQYIA85Flt5jd8Zf&typo=1>\nFollow Us on Twitter<http://twitter.com/n
 cxgroup>\n“Like” Us on Facebook<http://www.facebook.com/ncxgroup>\n\nFro
 m: Madeline Hammann <MHammann@landmarkventures.com<mailto:MHammann@landm
 arkventures.com>>\nDate: Wednesday\, May 5\, 2021 at 7:25 AM\nTo: Michae
 l Fitzpatrick <mfitzpatrick@ncxgroup.com<mailto:mfitzpatrick@ncxgroup.co
 m>>\nSubject: RE: CloudKnox discussion with NCX Group\n\nHi Mike\,\n\nHa
 ppy Wednesday!\n\nI am following up here to get this meeting with CloudK
 nox in the calendar\, did any of the below dates/times work on your end?
  Look forward to hearing from you!\n\nBest\,\nMaddie\n\nFrom: Madeline H
 ammann\nSent: Monday\, May 3\, 2021 3:55 PM\nTo: mfitzpatrick@ncxgroup.c
 om<mailto:mfitzpatrick@ncxgroup.com>\nSubject: RE: CloudKnox discussion 
 with NCX Group\n\nHi Mike\,\n\nHappy Monday\, I hope you had a nice week
 end!\n\nI am reaching out to get this call with CloudKnox in the calenda
 r\, below are some open time slots in the coming weeks:\n\n\n  *   Tuesd
 ay\, May 18th at 9:00am-11:00am ET or 5:00pm to 6:00pm ET\n  *   Wednesd
 ay\, May 19th at 9:00am-10:30am ET or 2:30pm-4:00pm ET\n  *   Thursday\,
  May 20th at 9:00am-10:30am ET or 12:30pm-4:00pm ET\n\nPlease let me kno
 w if any of these dates/times work on your end and I will send over the 
 calendar invitation. Just a reminder that all of these times are ET. Loo
 k forward to hearing from you!\n\nBest\,\nMaddie\n\n\nFrom: Avi Legmann 
 <alegmann@landmarkventures.com<mailto:alegmann@landmarkventures.com>>\nS
 ent: Monday\, May 3\, 2021 3:30 PM\nTo: mfitzpatrick@ncxgroup.com<mailto
 :mfitzpatrick@ncxgroup.com>\nCc: Madeline Hammann <MHammann@landmarkvent
 ures.com<mailto:MHammann@landmarkventures.com>>\; Aaliyah Griffin <agrif
 fin@landmarkventures.com<mailto:agriffin@landmarkventures.com>>\nSubject
 : CloudKnox discussion with NCX Group\n\nHello Mike\n\nFollowing our con
 versation and the previous mail\, attach some background material on Clo
 udKNox you can review before the intro call.\n\nMaddie will help schedul
 e the intro call with you – feel free to bring the relevant team members
  to these calls.\n\nRegards\n\nAvi\n\n=======\nCloudKnox is focused on f
 ixing and preventing privilege creep that has caused major breaches (for
  example\, last year a top 5 bank exposed 106MM credit cards because of 
 a misconfigured AWS permission).\n\nEvery cloud workload has 20\,000+ pe
 rmissions that can be enabled and all it takes is for 1 account to be ov
 erprovisioned with more access than needed to cause risk.  And because D
 evOps shifts infrastructure responsibility to the developer (who inheren
 tly prioritizes pushing out code quickly)\, it’s almost impossible to ge
 t privileges set right the first time.\n\nCloudKnox automatically maps a
 ll permissions across workloads in cloud infrastructure (AWS\, Azure\, G
 CP\, VMware) to identities to understand exactly who can do what – and t
 hen analyzes activity patterns to establish and enforce access policies 
 to constantly right-size with “just enough permission.”\n\nI’ve attached
  a few key updated documents:\n\n\n  *   Overview – describes the proble
 m and architecture of solution in detail\n  *   Top permissions risks – 
 outlines the impact of having too many permissions enabled and types of 
 attacks that CloudKnox mitigates\n  *   Sample Risk Assessment – this is
  an example of the output you would get of a complementary risk assessme
 nt\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
